## Scope

- focused `/lesson/active` presentation for Study, Recall and Choice;
- canonical progress/header/card/confidence hierarchy on compact mobile, medium/tablet and desktop;
- objective answer attempt/reveal states and explicit correct/incorrect semantics;
- Choice options shown immediately, with no Recall input or options toggle;
- safe lesson exit with progress explanation, focus trap and focus return;
- browser Back interception without duplicate review submission;
- Light/Dark semantic-token presentation, 200% zoom, reduced motion and no-horizontal-overflow support;
- keyboard and screen-reader semantics;
- contract, E2E, axe and Linux visual-regression coverage.

## Out of scope

- Lesson Result and next-block progression (#194);
- offline/sync/outbox redesign (#202);
- scheduler or review API changes;
- backend API changes;
- global architecture or legacy-style cleanup.

## Ownership boundaries

`LexigoPremiumApp` remains the owner of authentication, active-session loading, `lessonVersion`, server-controlled current position, review submission, completion, progress refresh, navigation lock and outbox integration. `ActiveLessonPresentation` is intentionally presentation-only: it receives state and callbacks and does not issue requests or calculate the next lesson position.

